  "description": "Overview The Departments of CSE (AI & ML), CSE (DS), and AI & ML at Vignan Institute of Technology & Science (VITS), Hyderabad, present HACKVIBE 2.0, a 24-hour national-level hackathon focused on building innovative, technology-driven solutions to real-world problems. Domains: AI, IoT, Cybersecurity Format: Offline, 24-hour hackathon Team Size: 3 members per team Registration Fee: ₹500 per team Prize Pool: ₹35,000 Date: 8th & 9th October 2026 Venue: Vignan Institute of Technology & Science, Hyderabad Eligibility Open to college students across India. Participants must register in teams of exactly 3 members. Process Register as a team of 3. Complete the registration and payment process. Develop a solution during the 24-hour hackathon. Submit the project within the specified deadline. Present and demonstrate the solution before the judging panel. Results will be announced after final evaluation. Evaluation Projects will be evaluated based on innovation, problem relevance, technical implementation, functionality, scalability, and presentation. Rules Each team must have exactly 3 members. A participant can be part of only one team. Plagiarism, fraudulent submissions, or intellectual property violations may result in disqualification. Teams must follow the event guidelines and code of conduct. Participants must submit and demonstrate their project within the specified timelines. The organizers reserve the right to disqualify teams violating the rules.",
