    "details": "<p><strong>Overview</strong></p>\n<p>The Departments of CSE (AI &amp; ML), CSE (DS), and AI &amp; ML at Vignan Institute of Technology &amp; Science (VITS), Hyderabad, present HACKVIBE 2.0, a 24-hour national-level hackathon focused on building innovative, technology-driven solutions to real-world problems.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Domains: AI, IoT, Cybersecurity</li>\n<li>Format: Offline, 24-hour hackathon</li>\n<li>Team Size: 3 members per team</li>\n<li>Registration Fee: ₹500 per team</li>\n<li>Prize Pool: ₹35,000</li>\n<li>Date: 8th &amp; 9th October 2026</li>\n<li>Venue: Vignan Institute of Technology &amp; Science, Hyderabad</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to college students across India. Participants must register in teams of exactly 3 members.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Process</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Register as a team of 3.</li>\n<li>Complete the registration and payment process.</li>\n<li>Develop a solution during the 24-hour hackathon.</li>\n<li>Submit the project within the specified deadline.</li>\n<li>Present and demonstrate the solution before the judging panel.</li>\n<li>Results will be announced after final evaluation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Evaluation</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Projects will be evaluated based on innovation, problem relevance, technical implementation, functionality, scalability, and presentation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each team must have exactly 3 members.</li>\n<li>A participant can be part of only one team.</li>\n<li>Plagiarism, fraudulent submissions, or intellectual property violations may result in disqualification.</li>\n<li>Teams must follow the event guidelines and code of conduct.</li>\n<li>Participants must submit and demonstrate their project within the specified timelines.</li>\n<li>The organizers reserve the right to disqualify teams violating the rules.</li>\n</ul>",
    "end_date": "2026-10-02T00:00:00+05:30",
